<title>UK: Standard Chartered sets $200 mln 10-yr step-up FRN.</title>
<headline>Standard Chartered sets $200 mln 10-yr step-up FRN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following subordinated structured floating-rate issue was announced by lead manager Goldman Sachs International.</p>
<p> BORROWER   STANDARD CHARTERED BANK</p>
<p> AMT	  $200 MLN  BASE	 3M-LIBOR  MATURITY     **DEC.06</p>
<p> TYPE	 FRN	 MARGIN    *+40 BP    PAY DATE    20.DEC.96</p>
<p> LAST MOODY A3 (SUB)  ISS PRICE  PAR	 FULL FEES   0.375</p>
<p> LAST S&amp;P   A- (SUB)  REOFFER    PAR</p>
<p> NOTES    **CALLABLE AT PAR ON COUPON DATES AFTER FIVE YEARS.</p>
<p>	     *MARGIN RISES TO 90 B.P. IN YEARS SIX TO 10.</p>
<p> LISTING    LONDON    DENOMS (K) 100	 SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 2</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  0.175     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
